  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Economic Recovery and Development (ERDA)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Pakistan):  .The $24-million, five-year Economic Recovery and Development.activity (ERDA) aims to expand environmentally sustainable, socially equitable,.and climate-resilient economic opportunities in Khyber Pakhtunkhwa (KP).province.  This goal will be achieved by strengthening and modernizing the.agriculture sector and promoting on- and off-farm micro-, small- and.medium-enterprises (MSMEs).  Additionally, ERDA will provide targeted.technical assistance to the Government of Khyber Pakhtunkhwa (GoKP) to maximize.the impact of planned public sector economic growth initiatives to build a.foundation for sustainable economic growth in the region.  In particular,.ERDA will support policy reforms to create an enabling environment for private.sector investments in high economic-growth potential sectors, including trade,.transport, health and education. Lack of economic opportunities is considered one of.the major drivers of extremism and instability in the KP region.  The activity will promote licit economic.activities and in doing so will contribute to stabilization and sustainable.economic development of the region. ERDA will also work with the GoKP to.help respond to the devastating 2022 floods by promoting agricultural recovery.and food security.  ERDA complements the GoKP&apos;s planned economic growth.investments under the Tribal Decade Strategy... ..This IM contributes $200,000 to the Gender earmark. .. ...</narrative>
  </description>
